    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Zadkiel was born to a family of hidden Sephardic Jews (conversos) who fled Iberia's expulsions to Brazil, and was drawn as a young rabbi-lawyer into the Schichiriel, a @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.phgt6OMwTAoAaKfR]{Lasombra} antitribu lineage practicing an abyssal, heretical Kabbalah that sought divinity through the negative emanations (qliphoth) of God. In 1803 the @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.phgt6OMwTAoAaKfR]{Lasombra} cardinal Charles Delmare (later Charles VI) annihilated the Schichiriel; Zadkiel alone survived by selling himself into Charles' service, then relocated to Mexico City decades later to become the city's leading teacher of abyss mysticism and @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.paths-of-enlightenment.JournalEntry.n1ghtP4thOfN1ght]{Path of Night}.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Zadkiel rarely resumes human form, preferring to stalk the city as a birdlike shadow. He counsels any Cainite who suffers under undeath regardless of sect, dissects the selfish passions of those he meets, and never commands another except in self-defense, believing every soul must find and endure its own choices. He maintains a cool, distant solidarity with fellow teacher-neutral Efra\u00edn Sortano and keeps five bound abyssal Retainers (Strength/Dexterity 5, Mental Traits 2 each) in the flooded well beneath his storm-drain haven.</p>",
    "notes": "Merit: Controllable Night Sight (sees in darkness/shadow as light; light obscures him as darkness; can toggle at will \u2014 see Clanbook: @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.phgt6OMwTAoAaKfR]{Lasombra}). Sire: Aron ben Aretz. Ratings above 5 from the original stat block have been capped to this system's 1-5 scale.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
